  "agent": "holmes-native",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. Pod `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` logs repeated `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire ...)` alongside memory pressure warnings.\n2. Deployment `billing-api` in `demo-apps` sets `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900`.\n3. Resource `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` in `ack-system` configured `idleClientTimeout: 600` via change CI-2452.\n\n### Ruled-out leads\n1. Pod crashes or OOMKills are ruled out because `billing-api` is Running with zero restarts.\n2. Load balancer idle timeout mismatch is ruled out because CI-2455 raised the ALB timeout (120s) and keep-alive (125s) consistently.\n\n### Root cause\nThe RDS DBProxy `idleClientTimeout` (600s) is shorter than `billing-api` connection pool idle timeout (900s), causing the proxy to drop idle connections prematurely (documented in RB-014 and INC-2024-0312).\n\n### Recommended action\nThe platform team should update `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` in `ack-system` to raise `idleClientTimeout` above 900s or remove it to restore the 1800s default.",
